# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets (munhub-web,
# web/wrangler.jsonc). Vite copies this file into dist/. Keep in sync with
# web/vercel.json.
#
# The API origin in the CSP below is the production one. A build against a
# different API (VITE_API_URL=…, e.g. staging) rewrites it in dist/_headers —
# see web/vite-plugins/api-origin-csp.ts and the plugin in web/vite.config.ts.
#
# CSP notes:
# - No inline scripts: the build emits only external module scripts, and
#   next-themes' anti-flash <script> is rendered as an inert
#   type="application/json" block (src/components/theme-provider.tsx), which a
#   CSP never evaluates, so no hash or nonce is needed.
# - style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' for index.html's <style> block, the <style>
#   next-themes injects for disableTransitionOnChange, and style attributes.
# - challenges.cloudflare.com is Cloudflare Turnstile.
# - static.cloudflareinsights.com is Cloudflare's own analytics beacon,
#   auto-injected into every HTML response on a proxied zone — not something
#   this app requests. Blocking it doesn't stop the injection, just breaks it
#   with a console error, so it's allowed rather than fought.
# - Permissions-Policy allows the camera for this origin only: the organizer
#   check-in panel scans delegate passes with it. camera=() would make every
#   getUserMedia call fail with no prompt the user could answer.
# - connect-src lists the production API. A build against another API (e.g.
#   staging's VITE_API_URL) gets that origin appended in dist/_headers by
#   vite-plugins/api-origin-csp.ts; don't hard-code other APIs here.
# - GuruPay (docs/payments/SPEC.md) is a redirect-based checkout
#   (window.location.assign to its hosted payment_url), not an embedded
#   widget/frame, so CSP's connect-src/frame-src don't govern the top-level
#   navigation itself. www.gurupaygateway.com is allowlisted in
#   connect-src/frame-src defensively anyway, in case the hosted page or a
#   future non-redirect integration step needs it.
#   Confirmed real domain (GuruPay dashboard, 2026-09-18): the API and the
#   hosted checkout page are both under www.gurupaygateway.com (payment_url
#   looks like https://www.gurupaygateway.com/pay/...) — api.gurupaygateway.com
#   does not resolve at all. See lib/payments/gurupay-adapter.ts.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self' https://api.munhub.in https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.gurupaygateway.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.gurupaygateway.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
